/** \file p4_algorithm.dox
 * \brief Developer guide to the P4 algorithm implementation.
 * \author Jared R. Males
 */

/** \addtogroup developer_p4_algorithm
 * @{
 *
 * `p4Reduce` dispatches either one normal reduction or repeated pixel-local evaluations for negative-companion
 * optimization. \ref mx::improc::P4Reduction::reduce "P4Reduction::reduce()" delegates the reduction to
 * \ref mx::improc::P4Reduction::regions "P4Reduction::regions()", which constructs annular geometry and temporal
 * selections before choosing the full-frame or pixel-local path.
 *
 * Each detector-pixel fit enters `P4Reduction::fitDetectorSearch()` to sample the target time series and predictor
 * matrix, then calls \ref mx::improc::P4PCA::calculate "P4PCA::calculate()" for
 * Gram construction, eigendecomposition, rank selection, and residual projection. Pixel-local processing schedules
 * only the unique detector fits needed by the requested sky stamp, but uses this same regression kernel.
 *
 * \section developer_p4_flow Processing diagram
 *
 * <div class="p4-algorithm-diagram">
 * <a href="p4_algorithm_processing.pdf" title="Open the P4 processing diagram as a PDF">
 * <img src="p4_algorithm_processing.svg" alt="Block diagram of P4 algorithm processing" />
 * </a>
 * </div>
 *
 * Click the diagram to open the vector PDF. The editable TikZ source is `doc/figures/p4_algorithm_processing.tex`.
 * The diagram follows the detector-frame science path and intentionally omits detailed memory management and error
 * handling.
 *
 * \section developer_p4_code_map Code map
 *
 * - `src/apps/p4Reduce.cpp`: application and negative-companion optimizer dispatch.
 * - `src/common/P4Reduction.cpp`: geometry, scheduling, regression orchestration, and final products.
 * - `src/common/P4PCA.cpp`: numerical PCA kernel.
 * - `src/common/P4PixelGrid.cpp` and `src/common/P4LocalProcessing.cpp`: detector and pixel-local geometry.
 * - `src/common/P4PSFModel.cpp`, `src/common/P4PSFReconstructor.cpp`, and `src/common/P4PSFFilter.cpp`: optional
 *   frozen-response products.
 *
 * @}
 */
